title: Dues and the Empty Treasury
subtitle: Set annual membership dues—or make one emergency appeal.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 200
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_fundraising_timer <= 0 and (month <= 2 or month >= 10 or resources <= party_income + 3 or early_election_risk >= 40)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_fundraising_timer = 12
card-image: img/poland/cards/fundraising.webp

= Dues and the Empty Treasury

State subvention follows the seats won at the last election. Everything else
must come from members, officeholders and sympathisers. Each January and July payout is
currently **[+ member_dues +] from dues** and **[+ seat_subvention +] from
subvention**.

- @maintain
- @lower
- @raise
- @emergency

@maintain
title: Keep dues where they are
subtitle: Each semiannual payout remains [+ party_income +].
on-arrival: public_trust += 1 if internal_dissent <= 20; organiser_energy += 1 if internal_dissent <= 20; news_headline = "The treasurer leaves annual dues unchanged"

The treasurer gets no miracle. A settled organisation can still use the
collection drive to update its member roll.

- #poland_card_finish

@lower
title: Lower membership dues
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource now. Each January/July payout falls by one; every caucus gets some relief.
choose-if: member_dues > 1 and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Dues are already at their floor, or the party cannot finance the transition.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.member_dues -= 1;
Q.party_income = Q.member_dues + Q.seat_subvention +
    (Number(Q.warsaw_mayoral_income_bonus) || 0);
for (const faction of Q.caucus_ids || Q.factions) {
    Q[faction + "_dissent"] -= 4;
}
Q.organiser_energy += 3;
Q.workers_support += 1;
Q.young_support += 1;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica lowers the price of membership";
!}

The immediate accounting is awkward, but local organisers stop explaining why
membership costs more precisely when household bills are rising.

- #poland_card_finish

@raise
title: Raise membership dues
subtitle: +1 resource now and +1 on each January/July payout. Higher levels burden the party's least affluent base.
choose-if: member_dues < 5
unavailable-subtitle: The treasurer refuses to push dues above the political ceiling.
on-arrival: {!
Q.member_dues += 1;
Q.party_income = Q.member_dues + Q.seat_subvention +
    (Number(Q.warsaw_mayoral_income_bonus) || 0);
Q.resources += 1;
Q.organiser_energy -= 2 + Math.max(0, Q.member_dues - 3);
Q.workers_support -= 1 + Math.max(0, Q.member_dues - 3);
Q.young_support -= 1;
Q.public_trust -= Math.max(0, Q.member_dues - 3);
Q.razem_dissent += 2;
Q.barons_dissent -= 1;
Q.news_headline = "Members are asked to finance a more expensive party";
!}

The treasury improves immediately. So does the list of members who quietly
decide that political commitment has become another monthly bill.

- #poland_card_finish

@emergency
title: Launch an emergency small-donor appeal
subtitle: +2 resources. The nationwide appeal cannot be repeated for sixteen months.
choose-if: emergency_fundraising_timer <= 0 and (resources <= 3 or early_election_risk >= 50 or pres_2020_active = 1 or (year = 2025 and month <= 6))
unavailable-subtitle: The donor list is exhausted, or there is no immediate campaign emergency to justify another national appeal.
on-arrival: emergency_fundraising_timer = 16; resources += 2; organiser_energy -= 4; public_trust -= 1; turnout_readiness += 1; news_headline = "A small-donor appeal covers the immediate shortfall"

Thousands of modest transfers arrive. So do unsubscribes, complaints and the
knowledge that the word “emergency” cannot be used every quarter.

- #poland_card_finish
